commit 71d73895245e858cd13936213c3ee28272a214a3
Author: Buu <buddingnewinsights@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 25 11:38:19 2026 +0700

    feat(protocol): setAnimation mutation (S12a)
    
    Single op carrying a numeric target StyleMap + transitionMs + optional
    easing (linear|easeIn|easeOut|easeInOut, default easeOut). Closed
    animatable-key set (width/height/minWidth/minHeight/padding/gap/
    borderRadius/fontSize/flexGrow/flexShrink/opacity) — unlike setStyle's
    forward-compatible open set, interpolation needs a real numeric render path
    so animating anything else is rejected on BOTH sides (TS decode =
    invalidShape; Rust retained apply = InvalidMutation). Each key must already
    hold a numeric value on the element (well-defined start). The target is
    merged into the static style at apply time so the end state sticks without
    further protocol traffic; the helper substitutes interpolated values per
    frame until the transition completes (next commit).
    
    Fixtures batch-animation-01.json parsed + round-tripped byte-identically by
    both suites (BTreeMap canonical key order — opacity before width).

